{
  "case_id": "2019-19-67",
  "document_hash": "2538dde01d454fb6bcbaa9e658ffe3774ab2f13ae128289981c55229d3cce8b4",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2019-19-67",
      "confidence": 0.96,
      "document_hash": "2538dde01d454fb6bcbaa9e658ffe3774ab2f13ae128289981c55229d3cce8b4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2538dde01d45-0000-0000",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 2,
        "start": 2
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The above-entitled matter came on for oral argument before the Supreme Court of the United States at 10:27 a.m."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "United States",
      "case_id": "2019-19-67",
      "confidence": 0.94,
      "document_hash": "2538dde01d454fb6bcbaa9e658ffe3774ab2f13ae128289981c55229d3cce8b4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2538dde01d45-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Respondent acknowledges that in the context of a criminal law, the terms \"encourage\" and \"induce\" can refer solely to acts that facilitate or solicit unlawful activity. That's the meaning that they have in the context of this criminal law."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Respondent",
      "case_id": "2019-19-67",
      "confidence": 0.93,
      "document_hash": "2538dde01d454fb6bcbaa9e658ffe3774ab2f13ae128289981c55229d3cce8b4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2538dde01d45-0000-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Yet, Respondent and her amici have identified no actual instances in which the statute has been applied to protected First Amendment activity or any concrete documented instances of chilling speech."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2019-19-67",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "2538dde01d454fb6bcbaa9e658ffe3774ab2f13ae128289981c55229d3cce8b4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2538dde01d45-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 6,
        "start": 6
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: You -- you would acknowledge, though, that there are situations in which this would be unconstitutional as applied?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2019-19-67",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2538dde01d454fb6bcbaa9e658ffe3774ab2f13ae128289981c55229d3cce8b4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2538dde01d45-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "So, if the -- if the defendant just says, well, I encourage you to stay here, that might not be enough, but, if the defendant says it 10 times in a forceful voice, that would be a violation?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2019-19-67",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2538dde01d454fb6bcbaa9e658ffe3774ab2f13ae128289981c55229d3cce8b4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2538dde01d45-0001-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "But what do you mean by \"substantial participation\"? Because I didn't really take that from your brief, so I'm a little bit confused as to where that's coming from."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
      "case_id": "2019-19-67",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2538dde01d454fb6bcbaa9e658ffe3774ab2f13ae128289981c55229d3cce8b4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2538dde01d45-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 43,
        "start": 43
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAVANAUGH: If the statute, just to be clear, if the statute said aid, abet or solicit, that would be constitutional?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Fleming",
      "case_id": "2019-19-67",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2538dde01d454fb6bcbaa9e658ffe3774ab2f13ae128289981c55229d3cce8b4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2538dde01d45-0002-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 43,
        "start": 43
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. FLEMING: It would not, Justice Kavanaugh, because of the civil/criminal issue we've been discussing. It would say aid, abet or solicit conduct that in itself is not criminal."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Fleming",
      "case_id": "2019-19-67",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2538dde01d454fb6bcbaa9e658ffe3774ab2f13ae128289981c55229d3cce8b4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2538dde01d45-0002-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 54,
        "start": 54
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. FLEMING: Absolutely, Mr. Chief Justice. And the fact that you would need to do that in order for it to be constitutional is a good indication that Congress did not mean for the statute to be read that way, which is why we think the easier opinion to write is an opinion that says we look at the text, we look at the context, and there's nothing in this subsection (iv) that suggests that Congress meant the kind of limited statute that Justice Breyer is proposing."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
      "case_id": "2019-19-67",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2538dde01d454fb6bcbaa9e658ffe3774ab2f13ae128289981c55229d3cce8b4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2538dde01d45-0002-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 60,
        "start": 60
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAVANAUGH: If Congress wrote a statute that said it is a crime to aid, abet, or solicit certain serious civil offenses, A, B, C, is that law on its face permissible?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2019-19-67",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2538dde01d454fb6bcbaa9e658ffe3774ab2f13ae128289981c55229d3cce8b4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2538dde01d45-0003-0004",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 63,
        "start": 63
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "These are not unusual or strange words to use in this context to mean what we are saying that they mean."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2019-19-67",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2538dde01d454fb6bcbaa9e658ffe3774ab2f13ae128289981c55229d3cce8b4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2538dde01d45-0003-0005",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 64,
        "start": 64
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "this statute, as I was discussing earlier with Justice Breyer, covers the facilitation, solicitation of a lot of actual criminal conduct, coming to and entering the United States unlawfully."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2019-19-67",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2538dde01d454fb6bcbaa9e658ffe3774ab2f13ae128289981c55229d3cce8b4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2538dde01d45-0003-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 65,
        "start": 65
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: -- what in reading this statute would give an average person notice of all of the limitations you're suggesting to us? Because I read \"encourage or induce an alien to come, enter, or reside in the U.S., knowing or in reckless disregard of the fact that such coming to, entry, or residence is or will be in violation of law,\" seems to me that all of the examples that were raised earlier, the hospital that's treating a child with -- an illegally present child with a disease, the church who provides worship to illegal aliens, all of the other examples that were given on their face to the common reader of those words would be a violation of the statute."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Feigin",
      "case_id": "2019-19-67",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2538dde01d454fb6bcbaa9e658ffe3774ab2f13ae128289981c55229d3cce8b4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2538dde01d45-0003-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 65,
        "start": 65
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. FEIGIN: Well, Your Honor, I don't think that is the standard -- I don't think that's the standard this Court applies that someone is ignorant of what those words mean in the context of the criminal law."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Feigin",
      "case_id": "2019-19-67",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2538dde01d454fb6bcbaa9e658ffe3774ab2f13ae128289981c55229d3cce8b4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2538dde01d45-0003-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 66,
        "start": 66
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. FEIGIN: -- we are using the principles of complicity and solicitation in a statute that is directed at large amounts of criminal activity to inform what these words mean here."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2019-19-67",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "2538dde01d454fb6bcbaa9e658ffe3774ab2f13ae128289981c55229d3cce8b4",
      "evidence_id": "ev-2538dde01d45-0003-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 67,
        "start": 67
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: Thank you, counsel. The case is submitted."
    },
